From 8bfb14a24d4357bce2982eeef55180fd8775ff67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:45:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(bedrock): show server creative items in a Bedrock tab

Build the Bedrock tab from the connected server catalog and hide unavailable item types in vanilla category tabs. Carry catalog entry identity and converted item model data through the Java creative UI so duplicate fallback items select the intended Bedrock stack. Minecraft keeps the display-items callback protected, so a small package bridge registers the tab without reflection.

Retain the exact native catalog entry and complete item snapshot through Java creative tabs. Match recipe-book tab entries by item definition before component parsing changes equality; derive group representatives without inventing variants. Respect the native maximum creative stack and avoid ambiguous same-Java-item transfer fallbacks. Catalog tests cover representative selection, exact identity and variant ambiguity.
